sops.workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner;
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner
   Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer;
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End.

Description:
Transportation Planner first establishes the closed-loop route (Fort Lauderdale → intermediate cities → return to Fort Lauderdale) within budget, using date-specific transport searches. Accommodation Planner then books stays for 2 people across valid nights, respecting hotel constraints. Simultaneously, Restaurant Planner selects non-repeating American/Chinese cuisine options per meal/day, while Attractions Planner curates free daily activities. Final Plan Summarizer validates all components against user constraints (budget, cuisine, closed loop) before outputting the integrated itinerary.
